  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Interior obligated $204M in FY2027 to date for federal contracts. The Department of the Interior recorded 1,977 awards at an average award size of $103K. The Department of the Interior's obligations are down 97.0% year over year. The Department of the Interior's recent fiscal totals contrast sharply with prior years: FY22 obligations were $6.5B, FY23 obligations were $7.6B, FY24 obligations were $8.1B, FY25 obligations were $6.6B, and FY26 obligations were $6.8B. The Department of the Interior concentrated FY2027 to date spending in Computer Systems Design Services with $49.5M, in Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction with $27.6M, in Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $24M, and in Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction with $21.3M. The Department of the Interior's top vendors in FY2027 to date include GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. with $38.7M and PAULSEN CONSTRUCTION LLC with $21.6M. The Department of the Interior's current-year totals are partial, as fiscal year to date reporting is incomplete.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed compared with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior obligated $204M in FY2027 to date, down 97.0% year over year. The Department of the Interior's FY22 through FY26 obligations ranged from $6.5B to $8.1B, then fell to $204M in FY27 to date. The Department of the Interior's award count is 1,977 with an average award size of $103K, reflecting current-year, partial totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors received the most FY2027 to date funding?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services received $49.5M, the largest NAICS category for FY2027 to date. The Department of the Interior's next largest categories include Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction with $27.6M, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $24M, and Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction with $21.3M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $38.7M and PAULSEN CONSTRUCTION LLC received $21.6M, the top two vendors for FY2027 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Interior spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior obligated $204M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Interior recorded 1,977 awards at an average award size of $103K, and obligations are down 97.0% year over year. FY22 obligations were $6.5B, FY23 obligations were $7.6B, FY24 obligations were $8.1B, FY25 obligations were $6.6B, and FY26 obligations were $6.8B."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Interior buy?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior buys IT, construction, engineering, forestry support, and environmental services. Computer Systems Design Services received $49.5M, Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction received $27.6M, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction received $24M, and Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction received $21.3M. The Department of the Interior also obligates funds in research and development, forestry support, and environmental consulting services."
